ve Disorder: high leukocyte count with normal differential is atypical for acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "Hyperparathyroidism: hypercalcemia alone would require less systemic symptom emphasis", "Infectious monocytosis: leukocytosis with constitutional symptoms but would require fever or neutrophilic shift"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Marked leukocytosis", "Hypercalcemia", "Elevated temperature (99.5°F)"]}, "branches": {"B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.13303315595579207, "posterior": 0.060987051979733545, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Subacute presentation and weight loss are inconsistent with most reactive leukocytoses but do not decisively support neoplastic causes due to limited specifici…"], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP is a key differentiator for reactive leukocytosis over CML and leukemoid reaction, moderately favoring B5. CML is strongly excluded due to low LAP…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.9, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.196479738027016, "posterior": 0.32426346406455253, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Subacute presentation and weight loss are inconsistent with most reactive leukocytoses but do not decisively support neoplastic causes due to limited specifici…"], "evidence_against": ["Absence of monoclonal protein and lytic lesions weakly contradicts multiple myeloma but does not exclude plasma cell disorders."], "unresolved_questions": [],